BT 1 0 0 1 0 53 Tm /F1 11 Tf 16 TL (RBAC is a security model in which access rights are assigned to roles rather than to individual) Tj T* (users. Each user is then given one or more roles, and inherits the permissions of those roles.) Tj T* (This keeps access consistent, makes administration simpler, and follows the principle of least) Tj T* (privilege, where users get only the access needed to do their work.) Tj T* ET
